# Commits to skip when attributing blame — mechanical, whitespace-only (or
# equivalent) changes whose line-by-line "blame" would otherwise bury the
# real last-meaningful-change commit under a reformat.
#
# Usage:
#   git blame --ignore-revs-file .git-blame-ignore-revs <path>
#
# Not auto-applied — git has no repo-committed way to turn this on globally
# for every clone, only a per-clone opt-in:
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
# (local to your own checkout's .git/config, so this file documents the
# convention rather than one clone's config forcing it on everyone else's).
# GitHub's own blame view reads this file directly with no config needed —
# see https://github.blog/changelog/2022-03-24-ignore-commits-in-the-blame-view-beta/
# — so the file alone already covers the primary (web) consumer; the git
# config line above is for anyone who also wants `git blame` on the command
# line to skip these by default in their own local checkout.

